# VRLeft input access (T1 mini keyboard, VID 1189 PID 8890)
#
# Gives the monitor daemon read access to the keypad's input event node so it
# can fire VRChat OSC messages from the six keys and the knob.
#
# Scoped to this vendor/product pair only. MODE=0666 is intentional so the
# tool works without a re-login or group change; see README "Security notes".
# Shift+1..0 on *your* keyboards needs no rule - log in with a session that
# can read /dev/input/event* (distros usually grant this to the "input" group).
SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1189", ATTRS{idProduct}=="8890", MODE="0666", GROUP="input", TAG+="uaccess"
